    {
      "object_id": "mathia_interpretation_47dd02b649e1ae43e0a3a7268db8f0b86cdf663338da5baeaa2d68b5d41e0d1f",
      "object_role": "interpretation",
      "proposed_content": "An L-function attached to arithmetic-geometric or automorphic data packages prime-indexed local factors in an Euler product; only in the stated half-plane of absolute convergence may that product be expanded into a series indexed by integral ideals. The product keeps the multiplicative local provenance visible, whereas the series compresses it into global coefficients suited to a different analytic representation. This construction does not by itself provide analytic continuation or a functional equation, and the claimed containment of arithmetic-geometric examples among automorphic ones is explicitly conjectural.",
